# The parent .clang-tidy, minus what doctest defeats. InheritParentConfig keeps everything else,
# so this file is the exception rather than a second check list.
#
#   bugprone-unchecked-optional-access
#     An access guarded by REQUIRE(x.has_value()) reads as unguarded here. REQUIRE is a doctest
#     macro that expands to a throwing call, and the check's dataflow analysis cannot follow
#     through the expansion to learn the value is there. The only rewrite it accepts is
#     value_or(), which supplies a fallback on a line the REQUIRE above has proved cannot need
#     one, so every site would say something weaker than it means.
#
#   clang-analyzer-*
#     The analyzer explores every path through each function, and a doctest case is one function
#     whose CHECK and REQUIRE macros each expand into a branch and an exception handler, so a long
#     case costs it minutes where every other check here takes seconds. What it hunts for (a null
#     dereference, a leak, a use after free) is what the suite's address and thread sanitizer runs
#     find in this code by executing it.
#
# Both stay on for src/core/, where an unguarded access would be a real defect, and where the
# tree passes clean under them.
---
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
  -clang-analyzer-*
